WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:50.660
[PIERRE screeches]

3
00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:53.800
<b>Overture</b>

4
00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:51.950
[CHOPPER]
I gotta save him.

5
00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:55.430
I've just gotta save him!

6
00:01:55.430 --> 00:01:58.100
He'll get eaten by skysharks
if I don't do something!

7
00:01:58.310 --> 00:01:59.430
[SHURA]
Judgment has been made!

8
00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:01.290
You were God, now you're
nothing! Nothing!

9
00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:03.000
Can't even defeat
a priest like me.

10
00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:04.130
[CHOPPER screams]

11
00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:06.590
I'll save you!

12
00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:10.050
[SHURA]
Ha! Ignorant little creature.

13
00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:13.010
You're diving into
your own watery grave.

14
00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:15.220
[CHOPPER groans]

15
00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:18.140
[PIERRE squawking]

16
00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:22.600
[SHURA]
And now for the
Sky Knight's noble steed.

17
00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:24.850
You no longer have a purpose.

18
00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.980
Follow your master!

19
00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:33.570
[PIERRE screeches]

20
00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:37.750
[squawking]

21
00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:39.460
[SHURA]
I do wish that I could be there

22
00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:42.630
to watch the life drain
from your faces.

23
00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:46.800
But alas, I have other
matters to attend to.

24
00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:53.060
Ah.

25
00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:56.700
I wonder if the three fugitives
have been captured yet.

26
00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:01.790
Could a well really be
that interesting?

27
00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:03.850
[ROBIN]
Yes. Don't you think it's odd

28
00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:06.690
that a well would be
stuck under a tree?

29
00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:09.900
The balance between civilization
and nature here is off.

30
00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:13.630
Well, unless we find a way
to cross this cloud river,

31
00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.870
we'll be stuck in this forest.

32
00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:21.750
[ZORO]
And we're still nowhere
near where we wanna be.

33
00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:23.120
[ROBIN]
It's like the
people who built this

34
00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.700
didn't know the tree
would grow to be so large.

35
00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:28.160
I've never seen
anything like it.

36
00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:29.660
[ZORO]
Hey, Nami!

37
00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:31.830
Can you see anything up there?

38
00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:39.130
[NAMI]
The island where God lives...

39
00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:40.750
Upper Yard.

40
00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:46.350
[ZORO]
Nami! Say somethin', would ya?

41
00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:47.300
What do you see?

42
00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:48.890
Hey, can you hear me?

43
00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:52.520
What do you think
she sees up there?

44
00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:55.060
[NAMI gasps]

45
00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:58.610
This island... can't be...

46
00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:04.460
[SATORI]
There's no way you can win!

47
00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:08.290
After all, I'm a priest,
and you all look so tired.

48
00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:11.840
Why don't you just end
this now and die? [laughs]

49
00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:13.800
My heart can't take
anymore of this.

50
00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:15.170
Too many surprises.

51
00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:17.050
Ow, it hurts.

52
00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:19.640
You'll be out of
options quite soon.

53
00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:22.510
It's sad really.

54
00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:25.430
Your little boat has nearly
reached the forest's exit

55
00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:29.520
and when that happens,
it's all over for you! [laughs]

56
00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:32.480
You'll have nowhere to go

57
00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:36.110
unless, of course,
you suddenly learn to fly!

58
00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:39.990
[LUFFY panting]

59
00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:42.990
[SATORI]
You'll wander around in
this terribly unfamiliar forest

60
00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:48.120
and die of exhaustion! [laughs]

61
00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:49.700
[LUFFY]
That won't...

62
00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:50.610
Hm?

63
00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:51.820
...happen!

64
00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:54.240
[SATORI]
Ha! Nice try!

65
00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:55.900
My turn now!

66
00:04:55.990 --> 00:04:57.570
[LUFFY gasps]

67
00:04:57.660 --> 00:04:59.160
[SATORI]
Sphere Dragon attack!

68
00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:01.300
You know you can't run forever.

69
00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:02.850
And wherever you stop,

70
00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:06.370
the fire-bomb ball will be
waiting to incinerate you!

71
00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:07.800
[SATORI laughs]

72
00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:09.600
[LUFFY panting]

73
00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:12.430
[laughs]

74
00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:16.720
[USOPP]
Good, looks like
we can still make it.

75
00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:18.590
I'll just leave things
here with you, Luffy!

76
00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:21.930
[LUFFY yelling]

77
00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:26.520
That tree... will not
give you any shelter.

78
00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:28.060
[LUFFY]
It's like he's reading my mind!

79
00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:31.530
Stay outta my head
and quit following me!

80
00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:32.970
[LUFFY grunts]

81
00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:34.600
[SATORI]
What are you doing?

82
00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:37.980
[LUFFY grunts]
A wire! What the...?

83
00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:41.690
Wait, this must be how
he controls the dragon!

84
00:05:41.890 --> 00:05:42.750
I'll just...

85
00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:44.000
No, stop!

86
00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:45.520
...do this!

87
00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:49.110
[gasps]
You ruined
my Sphere Dragon,

88
00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:50.970
you impudent little brat!

89
00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:52.470
Now you die!

90
00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:54.680
Get over here this
instance! [grunts]

91
00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:58.890
[yelling]

92
00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:00.640
[SATORI gasps]

93
00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:03.480
Let go of the dragon, you fool!

94
00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:25.410
[USOPP]
There it is!

95
00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:26.970
Yeah, I was right!

96
00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:29.590
I knew I could find the
way out of this place!

97
00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:31.720
Of course! This makes
perfect sense.

98
00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:33.640
Why didn't I think
of this sooner?

99
00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:36.940
When we fell before, it was
from a very high altitude.

100
00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:39.910
So it's only natural that the
exit be at the same height.

101
00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:41.480
And now that I know
where the exit is,

102
00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:44.640
the boat doesn't
really matter anymore.

103
00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:46.010
All right.

104
00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:48.060
That huge explosion
worries me. I'd better hurry.

105
00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:49.350
Game time.

106
00:06:50.470 --> 00:06:51.220
[USOPP]
Ow!

107
00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:57.190
[SATORI panting]

108
00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:58.650
That was close!

109
00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:00.860
That maniac must've
had a death wish!

110
00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:03.400
This isn't good. [pants]

111
00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:06.240
I've got to intensify
my training.

112
00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:10.470
I can't let a weakling like him
get the upperhand in a fight!

113
00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:13.050
Not even for a second!

114
00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:16.450
That might block me
from using my Mantra!

115
00:07:16.510 --> 00:07:17.310
[LUFFY]
You're right!

116
00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.330
[SATORI gasps]

117
00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:19.590
That was close!

118
00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:23.210
It's you! How are
you still alive?

119
00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:25.090
– [LUFFY chuckles]
– [SATORI screams]

120
00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:26.710
[SATORI]
Get off me!

121
00:07:27.490 --> 00:07:30.410
[SANJI]
Do not let him go, Luffy.

122
00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:31.870
You, too?

123
00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:33.830
Hey, Sanji, where've you been?

124
00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:36.210
I was out cold on
the forest floor!

125
00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:39.000
Where else would I
have been, you idiot?!

126
00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:41.420
But... that's beside the point.

127
00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:46.830
[SANJI]
See, the point is

128
00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:49.540
that you keep saying challenge
this and challenge that,

129
00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:51.710
which normally
wouldn't interest me.

130
00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:53.540
However, there are
two helpless ladies

131
00:07:53.630 --> 00:07:55.540
waiting for me to
come to their rescue,

132
00:07:55.630 --> 00:07:58.380
and I refuse to let them down.

133
00:07:58.460 --> 00:08:01.260
So I'm proposing this.

134
00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:03.170
And I think you'll like it.

135
00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:07.260
Ordeal of love.

136
00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:09.260
[SATORI]
This guy's an idiot, too!

137
00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:11.890
Unhand me this instant,
you maggots!

138
00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:14.320
[SATORI yelling]

139
00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:15.910
It's just not fair!

140
00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:19.370
You have no honor,
ganging up two against one!

141
00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:22.420
[SANJI]
We have no honor?

142
00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:26.980
You creeps kidnapped our friends

143
00:08:27.050 --> 00:08:29.510
and tried to murder a
beautiful young angel.

144
00:08:29.590 --> 00:08:32.550
And you accuse us of
not having any honor?

145
00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:33.680
[SATORI whimpers]

146
00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:35.140
I've been thinking.

147
00:08:35.220 --> 00:08:37.180
It's pretty amazing that you
can predict our movements.

148
00:08:37.270 --> 00:08:39.390
But what good is that...

149
00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:42.830
...if you do can't anything
to avoid 'em, huh? [chuckles]

150
00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:44.420
[SATORI screams]

151
00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:46.140
[SATORI]
Stop! Stop, I said!

152
00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:47.350
Are you listening?

153
00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:49.180
How dare you disobey me!

154
00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:51.310
I'm a priest in God's service!

155
00:08:51.390 --> 00:08:55.220
Not being judged by me is a
first-degree crime in Skypiea!

156
00:08:55.310 --> 00:08:56.310
Let me go!

157
00:08:56.390 --> 00:08:57.890
Now listen here!

158
00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:02.150
Attacking me means you declare
war on the Almighty God Eneru!

159
00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:03.470
I got a question.

160
00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:05.680
Do you ever cook?

161
00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:07.860
Well, you don't have
to be a chef to know

162
00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:11.030
which dish is best served cold.

163
00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:13.290
[SATORI screams]

164
00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:15.910
You know, this dish is
really quite simple.

165
00:09:16.050 --> 00:09:17.340
Step one:

166
00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:20.470
season the main course
with a smattering of defeat.

167
00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:23.030
[SANJI grunts]

168
00:09:24.900 --> 00:09:27.280
Then, you must brutally
and without hesitation

169
00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:28.610
tenderize the meat.

170
00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:30.780
[SATORI screams]
No! You can't do this!

171
00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:32.450
No!

172
00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:37.370
No! Please! No, don't hurt me!

173
00:09:37.460 --> 00:09:39.380
[SATORI screams]

174
00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:42.040
[SANJI]
Delicious!

175
00:09:42.130 --> 00:09:48.130
[yelling]

176
00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:52.040
[WYPER]
So Gan Fall, the former God,

177
00:09:52.120 --> 00:09:54.540
made his way into
the Upper Yard alone.

178
00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:59.120
[AISA whimpers]

179
00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:07.250
[screams]

180
00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:09.590
What's the matter, Aisa?

181
00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:11.550
Two voices. They're gone.

182
00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:12.720
What did you say?

183
00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:14.840
Huh? Your Mantra?

184
00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:18.640
Yes. It just happened.

185
00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:19.720
[WYPER growls]

186
00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:23.280
You're saying that
you heard two voices

187
00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:25.100
and then they
disappeared suddenly?

188
00:10:25.190 --> 00:10:27.060
You need to be honest with me.

189
00:10:27.150 --> 00:10:28.560
Is this true?

190
00:10:28.650 --> 00:10:31.070
[AISA exhales]

191
00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:32.820
I assume that's 'yes.'

192
00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:33.820
We should believe her.

193
00:10:33.870 --> 00:10:35.040
Ever since she was born,

194
00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:37.060
she has been able to use
her ability of Mantra

195
00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:39.970
to sense people, even those
who are far away from her.

196
00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:42.910
There's no mistaking her gift.

197
00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:44.250
You sure you don't hear them?

198
00:10:44.350 --> 00:10:45.350
They're not there anymore?

199
00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:48.380
Yeah. I think it's stopped.

200
00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:49.880
But...

201
00:10:49.970 --> 00:10:52.090
It seemed like Gan Fall was
fighting a priest and they...

202
00:10:52.190 --> 00:10:52.980
Killed each other?

203
00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:54.770
Nicely done, old man.

204
00:10:54.850 --> 00:10:56.350
There're only three left now.

205
00:10:56.430 --> 00:10:58.430
Which is good for us.

206
00:11:01.190 --> 00:11:04.440
I guess Heaven's actually
answered our prayers.

207
00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:08.070
It's time for us to crush those
priests once and for all.

208
00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:09.780
Yeah!

209
00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:11.240
On your feet!

210
00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:13.350
We're launching a full scale
attack on the Upper Yard.

211
00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:14.600
[OTHERS grunt]

212
00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:18.530
[LAKI]
Hm?

213
00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:20.520
Wyper still makes you
nervous, doesn't he?

214
00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:22.950
You have to grow up
sooner or later.

215
00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:25.240
[AISA gasps]

216
00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:29.270
[groans]
Laki, wait, please!

217
00:11:29.350 --> 00:11:30.520
What is it?

218
00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:32.940
It wasn't Gan Fall who
defeated that priest!

219
00:11:33.030 --> 00:11:34.700
There are others on
that side of the island

220
00:11:34.780 --> 00:11:36.410
and they're the
ones that did it!

221
00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:37.910
[LAKI]
Other people?

222
00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:40.990
You mean the ones who entered
Skypeia from the Blue Sea?

223
00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:44.330
I don't know who,
but they're really scary to me.

224
00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:45.160
So...

225
00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:46.390
...be careful.

226
00:11:47.590 --> 00:11:48.340
[sighs]

227
00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:50.350
[LAKI]
I'll try.

228
00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:53.390
Now be a good girl
and hand over your bag.

229
00:11:53.470 --> 00:11:54.810
[AISA]
No! I can't!

230
00:11:54.890 --> 00:11:57.940
This is my special secret bag!
It has treasure in it!

231
00:11:58.020 --> 00:12:00.020
I know that.

232
00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:01.690
[AISA groans]

233
00:12:01.770 --> 00:12:05.150
And it will have even more
inside when I bring it back.

234
00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:06.610
– Yeah?
– Yeah.

235
00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:15.330
[CHOPPER groans, gasps]

236
00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:19.760
[CHOPPER]
What's going on?

237
00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:21.010
I'm alive!

238
00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:24.720
What happened? [pants]

239
00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:27.730
Sky Knight!

240
00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:31.420
Hey! Doc! Oh! Wait, that's me.

241
00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:32.920
[GAN FALL groans]

242
00:12:33.010 --> 00:12:34.880
He's alive. That's good.

243
00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:40.410
[CHOPPER]
This makes no sense.
I jumped in after him.

244
00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:43.330
I figured we'd
sink to our deaths.

245
00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:45.700
I wonder who could have
pulled us out of there?

246
00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:50.920
[gasps]
Hey. What was that?

247
00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:53.750
Hello? Is someone there?

248
00:12:54.800 --> 00:12:56.550
[gasps, screams]

249
00:12:56.630 --> 00:12:57.630
[groans]

250
00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:00.390
[CHOPPER screams]

251
00:13:00.470 --> 00:13:04.220
[BIRD squawks]

252
00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:05.890
[CHOPPER gasping]

253
00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:09.310
– [BIRDS squawking]
– [CHOPPER screaming]

254
00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:11.940
But why?

255
00:13:14.420 --> 00:13:15.590
Enough with the mystery, Nami!

256
00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:18.340
Spit it out!
Tell us what you saw!

257
00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:20.590
[NAMI]
Quit ordering me around
and just do what I say!

258
00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:23.850
We have to get to the
seashore...[screams]

259
00:13:23.890 --> 00:13:25.800
Would one of you please help me?

260
00:13:25.890 --> 00:13:26.930
[ZORO]
You're the leader.

261
00:13:27.010 --> 00:13:28.680
Why don't you help yourself?

262
00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:29.750
The seashore?

263
00:13:29.770 --> 00:13:30.850
[NAMI]
Yes.

264
00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:32.140
It's the only way we
can get close enough

265
00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:34.560
to check this thing out.

266
00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:36.890
[ZORO yelling]

267
00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:38.230
'Cause to be honest,

268
00:13:38.310 --> 00:13:41.270
I won't believe what I saw
until I see it up close.

269
00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:43.540
[SANJI]
He couldn't have
shut up any sooner.

270
00:13:43.540 --> 00:13:45.210
– [USOPP] Hey! Guys!
– [LUFFY] Huh?

271
00:13:45.290 --> 00:13:46.580
Luffy! Sanji!

272
00:13:46.670 --> 00:13:48.670
I found the boat, but you
gotta move! I'm serious!

273
00:13:48.750 --> 00:13:50.000
If we don't get to it right now,

274
00:13:50.090 --> 00:13:52.630
we're gonna be stuck
on this stinkin' island!

275
00:13:52.710 --> 00:13:54.090
[SANJI]
I guess Usopp's okay.

276
00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:56.980
[LUFFY]
He's yelling
something about the boat.

277
00:13:57.050 --> 00:13:58.970
[USOPP pants]
Kick it into gear!

278
00:13:59.050 --> 00:14:02.060
The boat's leaving this place
and we gotta get on it now!

279
00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:04.560
[pants]
Get up here!

280
00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:05.980
You just hold on to my body.

281
00:14:06.060 --> 00:14:06.900
Your what?

282
00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:07.980
Here goes.

283
00:14:08.090 --> 00:14:13.840
Usopp... [yelling]

284
00:14:19.350 --> 00:14:21.060
Now that's what I
call marksmanship!

285
00:14:21.140 --> 00:14:23.850
[LUFFY]
Ha! Usopp, you're my hero!

286
00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:26.360
[USOPP]
Do you try to kill
all your heroes like that?

287
00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:27.790
[LUFFY]
I don't think so.

288
00:14:27.790 --> 00:14:29.300
I'm surprised you
pulled this off.

289
00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:32.130
Yeah? Well, no more
underestimating me!

290
00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:33.470
[ALL]
– Huh? Uh...
– Huh? Uh...

291
00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:34.510
The rope is tightening!

292
00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:36.640
– [LUFFY] Oh, no!
– Hold on!

293
00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:38.430
[ALL yelling]

294
00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:45.020
[ALL groaning]

295
00:14:47.090 --> 00:14:47.790
That... hurt so bad.

296
00:14:47.790 --> 00:14:50.040
[SANJI]
I will never
let you forget this.

297
00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:52.870
You know...

298
00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:56.330
...I could've stretched my
arm and grabbed the boat.

299
00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:59.330
[USOPP]
Look, we're on the
boat and out of the forest.

300
00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:00.790
That's all that matters.

301
00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:02.420
[USOPP gurgling]

302
00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:08.680
[GEDATSU]
Satori has fallen.

303
00:15:08.730 --> 00:15:10.490
Losing control over his Mantra

304
00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:13.360
only shows his
inexperience with it.

305
00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:16.490
It seems the intruders this
time are from the Blue Sea,

306
00:15:16.570 --> 00:15:18.700
but they behave strangely.

307
00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:21.530
The sacrifices are now
moving around freely as well.

308
00:15:21.530 --> 00:15:23.690
However, even if we
leave them alone,

309
00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:26.450
they won't find their
way off this island.

310
00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:29.870
More importantly...

311
00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:36.540
<b>"Sky Punk" Gedatsu
Skypiean Priest</b>

312
00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:40.420
[HOLY THE DOG panting]

313
00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:43.710
[OHM]
Do you hear the voice
of a sorrowful warrior, Holy?

314
00:15:43.820 --> 00:15:45.280
[woofs]

315
00:15:45.360 --> 00:15:47.450
[OHM]
It doesn't matter how
many times we walk this road.

316
00:15:47.530 --> 00:15:49.450
Things always end the same.

317
00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:53.330
Shura defeated Gan Fall, but the
Ordeal of Spheres was broken.

318
00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:56.470
That's where luck will end
for our new challengers.

319
00:15:56.560 --> 00:16:00.100
For them to attempt to see God
is insolence at its greatest,

320
00:16:00.190 --> 00:16:01.780
and their punishment at my hands

321
00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:05.440
will have things a bit unsettled
this evening in the Upper Yard.

322
00:16:05.320 --> 00:16:09.820
<b>"Sky Breeder" Ohm
Skypiean Priest</b>

323
00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:09.820
o one here gets out alive.

324
00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:19.290
<b>"Sky Rider" Shura
Skypiean Priest</b>

325
00:16:09.910 --> 00:16:11.580
\[FUZA screeches]

326
00:16:11.660 --> 00:16:14.580
\[SHURA] The ones who escaped
sacrifice are off my list.

327
00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:16.490
\It seems there are
others roaming around

328
00:16:16.570 --> 00:16:19.280
\who are more worthy of my anger!

329
00:16:43.510 --> 00:16:45.560
All of you, listen up!

330
00:16:45.610 --> 00:16:48.650
Today we catch Upper Yard
at her most vulnerable.

331
00:16:48.780 --> 00:16:51.490
This is the opportunity
of a lifetime.

332
00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:52.910
We move full speed ahead

333
00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:55.540
and don't stop until
we reach God's Shrine!

334
00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:57.710
And do not fear Eneru!

335
00:16:57.790 --> 00:17:00.960
The Great Warrior Kalgara
is our one and only savior!

336
00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:03.090
Only to him are we true!

337
00:17:06.050 --> 00:17:07.130
[WYPER]
Braham!

338
00:17:07.300 --> 00:17:08.050
Ready!

339
00:17:08.120 --> 00:17:08.870
[WYPER]
Kamakiri!

340
00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:09.920
[KAMAKIRI]
Hmph.

341
00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:10.920
[WYPER]
Genbou!

342
00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:11.790
[grunts]

343
00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:12.880
[WYPER]
Laki!

344
00:17:12.960 --> 00:17:14.000
Right.

345
00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:15.000
[WYPER]
Be careful.

346
00:17:15.310 --> 00:17:16.640
We split up here.

347
00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:23.100
[WYPER]
We vow to the
Great Warrior Kalgara

348
00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:25.390
to light the fire of Shandora!

349
00:17:25.470 --> 00:17:28.060
[SHANDORIAN WARRIORS cheer]

350
00:17:31.770 --> 00:17:32.900
[GEDATSU, OHM, SHURA]
– So the Shandorian's
– So the Shandorian's

351
00:17:32.980 --> 00:17:34.650
have come for a fight?

352
00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:40.630
[gasps]

353
00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:42.920
[NAMI]
Speaks for itself pretty well.

354
00:17:43.010 --> 00:17:45.550
Look at it. It's almost unreal.

355
00:17:47.050 --> 00:17:48.930
[NAMI]
But it's no fairy tale.

356
00:17:49.450 --> 00:17:51.040
[ZORO]
That doesn't make any sense.

357
00:17:51.120 --> 00:17:53.500
Why would this be here?
It looks exactly the same.

358
00:17:53.580 --> 00:17:54.830
It's like a copy.

359
00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:56.350
[ROBIN]
But it's not.

360
00:17:56.530 --> 00:17:57.870
[ZORO]
How do you figure?

361
00:17:57.950 --> 00:18:00.200
This is the other half
of what we saw before.

362
00:18:00.280 --> 00:18:01.400
[ZORO]
Go on.

363
00:18:01.490 --> 00:18:03.570
It's bugged me for a while.

364
00:18:03.650 --> 00:18:07.620
Why is it that we walk on soil
here instead of island cloud?

365
00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:08.990
This dirt.

366
00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:10.540
There's nothing in the makeup
of the White White Sea

367
00:18:10.620 --> 00:18:12.830
that would allow
for its existence.

368
00:18:12.910 --> 00:18:14.910
So... the ground that
we're walking on

369
00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:17.420
shouldn't exist up here.

370
00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:20.840
Upper Yard was originally
on the ground.

371
00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:23.750
[NAMI]
I knew that house
was off when I saw it.

372
00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:26.500
Thing is, it's a
two-story house,

373
00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:30.300
and there was no staircase
leading up to the second story.

374
00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:34.220
And what would make you build
a house on the edge of a cliff?

375
00:18:34.310 --> 00:18:38.730
But then again,
it wasn't a cliff at all.

376
00:18:38.930 --> 00:18:41.140
[LUFFY, USOPP]
– Whoa! Amazing!
– Whoa! Amazing!

377
00:18:41.390 --> 00:18:42.930
[ZORO grunts]
Look closer.

378
00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:44.810
It's really unattractive.

379
00:18:44.950 --> 00:18:47.950
A guy's gotta have some serious
guts to build a house that ugly.

380
00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:48.830
[CHOPPER]
What's that?

381
00:18:48.910 --> 00:18:50.240
[screams]

382
00:18:50.280 --> 00:18:52.620
[LUFFY]
This isn't a palace at all!

383
00:18:57.160 --> 00:19:01.370
[NAMI]
This is the half of the
island that was ripped away.

384
00:19:03.460 --> 00:19:06.290
[NAMI]
This island
used to be part of Jaya.

385
00:19:08.510 --> 00:19:11.010
[ZORO]
So what that means
is a few hundred years back,

386
00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:12.890
the island below
us split in half

387
00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:15.210
and one side of it
rose into the sky.

388
00:19:15.290 --> 00:19:17.880
[SOUTH BIRD squawks]

389
00:19:18.110 --> 00:19:20.150
[ZORO]
Either of you know
how that coulda happened?

390
00:19:21.230 --> 00:19:22.690
[SOUTH BIRDS squawking]

391
00:19:22.780 --> 00:19:24.320
They're... South Birds.

392
00:19:24.400 --> 00:19:26.740
A whole flock of 'em.

393
00:19:26.820 --> 00:19:28.120
They're huge.

394
00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:30.200
I didn't know they got so big.

395
00:19:48.100 --> 00:19:49.810
[USOPP laughs]
All right.

396
00:19:49.890 --> 00:19:52.690
Zoro, would you wake up already?

397
00:19:52.770 --> 00:19:55.020
Huh? You're a dead man.

398
00:19:56.020 --> 00:19:59.230
Sounds ridiculous,
but that's the best I can do.

399
00:19:59.890 --> 00:20:01.060
[SANJI]
No singing!

400
00:20:01.140 --> 00:20:05.980
[SOUTH BIRD squawking]

401
00:20:07.030 --> 00:20:10.320
[NAMI]
The City of Gold that
Noland discovered on the ground

402
00:20:10.400 --> 00:20:13.200
didn't sink into the
ocean like he guessed.

403
00:20:16.450 --> 00:20:17.820
This part of Jaya...

404
00:20:18.870 --> 00:20:22.670
It's been floating in
the sky for 400 years!
